Titles an X11 window that has no name with its WM_CLASS instance.

xwayland-satellite gives the compositor a window's WM_CLASS class as its
app id and its WM_NAME or _NET_WM_NAME as its title, and drops the
instance. A program that names each of its windows only by instance,
under one shared class and with no name, as Tuple does (tuple-screen and
tuple-webcams, both of class Tuple), reaches the compositor as several
windows with the same app id and no title, which no window rule can tell
apart. Such a window now goes by its instance as its title, until a name
set later takes its place. A WM_CLASS holding a class alone leaves the
window untitled, as before.

